  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "One past tense for two Spanish ones",
     "texto": [
      "The **pretérito perfeito** covers both «I ate» and «I have eaten». Portuguese does not use a compound tense for that: **Já comi** = I have already eaten. **Ontem comi peixe** = yesterday I ate fish."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How it is formed",
     "texto": [
      "You remove -ar, -er or -ir and add the endings. They are very similar to the Spanish ones.",
      "Note the «we» form of -ar verbs: in Portugal it takes an accent, **falámos**, to distinguish it from the present «falamos»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
